    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Alex's Skateboarding Webpage\r\n\r\nAlex wants to make a webpage about skateboarding but doesn't know how to write HTML or CSS. Instead, they've provided you with a description and a potential screenshot:\r\n\r\n> \"I want to make a webpage about skateboarding because it's my favorite hobby. I want it to feel like two separate parts — history and styles. Both parts should have a color so they look different from the rest of the page.\"\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://images.code.org/b7ea579e9e1119e7e9b886c247c9d891-image-1774410124636.png\" style=\"width: 40%\" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n**Do This:**\r\n1) Use AI tutor to help build this page. Ask it to make changes to this page step-by-step.\r\n    - Be specific about the elements, sizes, borders, and which elements they apply to\r\n2) Keep prompting until the webpage it's \"close enough\" to their vision!\r\n    - It doesn't have to perfectly match the image, but try to get it close to the style and layout!\r\n\r\nOnce you've compared your result to Alex's vision: press the Continue button!\r\n\r\n**Hint:** This puzzle involves `<section>` and `<h2>` tags in HTML, and the `background-color` and `color` properties in CSS.",
